IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, THE ROUTE TO ENFORCEMENT GATHERED BY HAND (ss 1, 2 and 7).
--
-- Ruling E1 (2026-11-04), option B as guidance for hand-gathering only: where several sections bear on one legal
-- effect, each section answers on its own (option C) and a reader who wants one answer may gather them by hand in
-- plain L4.  This module is that gathering for "the third party may enforce the term".  It holds no new law: it
-- takes the ANSWERS of the section rules as inputs and combines them.
--   * s 1(2) restriction applies    : JUST TRUE bars (the Act does not apply to the contract).
--   * s 2(1) the third party may enforce the term (the two routes).
--   * s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified.
--   * s 2(4) NOTHING means the enforcement is in accordance with the other terms of the contract; JUST FALSE bars.
--   * s 7(1) to (5): JUST FALSE bars; NOTHING means the contract is outside that exception, and the exception does not
--     bar.  That reading of a NOTHING rests on the facts for each exception being plain yes/no answers (fork G3).
-- JUST TRUE: nothing bars and both of s 2(1)'s conditions are met.  JUST FALSE: some provision says no.  NOTHING
-- otherwise, which includes a restriction of s 1(2) that cannot be decided on its date.
-- JUST FALSE is "the Act gives no right to enforce on these facts"; it is not a finding that the contract has no
-- other force.  Section 8(1) leaves any right or remedy apart from the Act in place.

-- src:41 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), this Act does not apply in relation to a
-- src:42 | contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- src:43 | 1 January 2002.
-- src:61 | 2.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person who is not a
-- src:62 | party to a contract (called in this Act a third party) may, in the third
-- src:63 | party’s own right, enforce a term of the contract if —
-- src:74 | (3) The third party must be expressly identified in the contract by
-- src:75 | name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description,
-- src:76 | but need not be in existence when the contract is entered into.
-- src:78 | (4) This section does not confer a right on a third party to enforce a
-- src:79 | term of a contract otherwise than subject to and in accordance with
-- src:80 | any other relevant terms of the contract.
-- src:260 | 7.—(1) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the
-- src:261 | case of a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other
-- src:262 | negotiable instrument.
-- src:264 | (2) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of
-- src:265 | any contract binding on a company and its members under section 39
-- src:266 | of the Companies Act 1967.
-- src:268 | (3) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of
-- src:269 | any registration document of a limited liability partnership registered
-- src:270 | under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 or any limited
-- src:271 | liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act.
-- src:275 | (4) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party to enforce
-- src:276 | any term of a contract of employment against an employee.
-- src:278 | (5) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case
-- src:279 | of —
-- src:281 | (a) a contract for the carriage of goods by sea; or
-- src:283 | (b) a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for
-- src:284 | the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of
-- src:285 | the appropriate international transport convention,
-- src:287 | except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third
-- src:288 | party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract.
@ref ss 1(2), 2(1), 2(3), 2(4) and 7(1) to (5) (src:41-43) (src:61-63) (src:74-80) (src:260-288)
GIVEN `the restriction in s 1(2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under s 2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under s 2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under s 2(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answers under s 7(1) to (5)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, through s 1(2)): "this Act does not apply in relation to a contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002"
        IF `the restriction in s 1(2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (through s 2(1)): "may, in the third party's own right, enforce a term of the contract if — (a) ...; or (b) ..."
        IF `the answer under s 2(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a condition of the right, judgment call QB, through s 2(3)): "The third party must be expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description"
        IF `the answer under s 2(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, through s 2(4)): "This section does not confer a right on a third party to enforce a term of a contract otherwise than subject to and in accordance with any other relevant terms of the contract."
        IF `the answer under s 2(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, through s 7(1) to (5)): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of ..."
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) `the answers under s 7(1) to (5)` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the restriction in s 1(2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `the answer under s 2(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the answer under s 2(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a restriction of s 1(2) that the text does not decide (a contract of 1 July 2002), or an answer of s 2(1) or (3) that has not been stated
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
